# Context compaction · agent checkpoints

## Problem

Long 2m-trading chats burn cache tokens. Critical state must survive a **new chat**.

## Critical data (MySQL `agent_checkpoints`)

Packed by `mcp-lighter/agent_checkpoint.py`:

- `_agent_trade_state.json`
- `_lit_session_state.json`
- `_tg_control.json`
- slim `_agent_tick_brief` (position, ROC, session, decision_hint, report stub)
- handoff markdown → `_agent_handoff.md`
- rotate timer → `_agent_rotate_state.json`

Autosave: every ~10m from `agent_tick_brief.py` (`reason=auto`). Keep last ~80 rows.

## Telegram (instant, no agent queue)

Commands (live in `telegram_bot.py`):

- `rotate` / `новый чат` / `checkpoint` / `обрезать` → save + TG bootstrap text

Auto heavy nudge: schtask brief runs `maybe_heavy_notify` — if **>90m** since last load/rotate (cooldown 30m) → save + TG with paste commands. Does **not** open IDE chat.

## When to rotate (cut context)

Do a **save + ask user / TG** when any of:

- Chat is long / tooling-heavy and idle ticks still cost a lot (cache reads huge)
- User asks to «обрезать контекст» / «новый чат» / «checkpoint» / TG `rotate`
- Before a risky flip if state must not be lost

Commands (cwd `mcp-lighter`):

```bash
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe agent_checkpoint.py rotate --source agent
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe agent_checkpoint.py heavy-check --force
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe agent_checkpoint.py handoff --latest
```

If chat feels heavy: run `heavy-check --force` (or `rotate`) — user gets TG; tell them to open a **new** Cursor chat.

## New chat bootstrap

```bash
cd mcp-lighter
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe agent_checkpoint.py load --latest --print-handoff
```

Restores JSON files + prints handoff + resets heavy timer. Then continue `/loop 2m` and read `_agent_tick_brief.json` as usual.

Also: `list --limit 20`, `load --id N`.

## Do not

- Do not try to delete Cursor transcript from tools — rotation = new chat + DB load
- Do not put secrets (`.env` keys) into checkpoints
- Do not claim TG can open a Cursor IDE chat — only save + instructions
